("v158", "type", "Sequence")
("v159", "type", "String")
("v159", "scalar", "The route into this problem began with satire. MoreWrong places elaborate intellectual machinery beside recognizable failures of ordinary responsibility. One narrator attempts to make complaints about his conduct disappear into statistical objections. Another treats the reputational consequences of an injury as though they have already settled the obligation to apologize. A landlord imagines better-informed tenants endorsing his preferred rent increase. Each joke allows the speaker's preferred framework to become an instrument for overruling the people affected by him. (")
("v158", "item", "v159")
