("v228", "type", "String")
("v228", "scalar", "A framework can therefore be accurate about the quantities it includes and misleading about the situation as a whole. If it represents preferences but has no place for intimidation, it may describe accommodation as consent. If it records an apology but cannot represent the money still owed, it may announce repair while a loss persists. If it counts participation but ignores the cost of leaving, it may interpret dependence as endorsement. The omission changes what the framework permits its users to see.")
("v227", "item", "v228")
("v226", "value", "v227")
