("v418", "type", "Sequence")
("v419", "type", "String")
("v419", "scalar", "Satire supplies candidates for those erased differences. It does not prove the correct replacement model. A joke can reveal a blindness while introducing one of its own. The productive response is to ask what the joke makes newly observable, which decisions that distinction should affect, and what evidence would support the resulting claim. This treats satire as a source of counterexamples rather than as a final court.")
("v418", "item", "v419")
("v417", "value", "v418")
