("v930", "type", "String")
("v930", "scalar", "The theological reading adds something different from another administrative level. In a Christian reading, a human institution's authority is not identical with God, and its account of its mission is not identical with divine judgment. That distinction can restrain an institution's claim to finality. It can also be abused when leaders treat their own interpretation as the voice that no one is entitled to challenge. The model records such an appeal as a person's attributed claim. It does not represent God as a node, a utility term, or an enforcement device.")
("v929", "item", "v930")
("v928", "value", "v929")
