("v959", "scalar", "In 1 Samuel 12, Samuel publicly invites testimony about property taken, oppression, and bribery, and offers restoration. That scene gives our discussion another blueprint: an authority can be asked to answer for specific acts and resources. Yet a public invitation does not, by itself, tell us what it cost anyone to respond. Asking whether witnesses could speak safely is a question we bring to the scene, not a detail the passage settles through a modern audit. (")
("v958", "item", "v959")
