("v979", "scalar", "Mark's account of leadership turns toward service, and Philippians describes Christ's self-humbling in the form of a servant. These provide a theological vocabulary for authority that relinquishes advantage. They do not license a leader to demand self-emptying from everyone below them. The question for institutional design is what the holder of power actually gives up, and whether the people served remain free to say that the service has failed. (")
