("v1019", "scalar", "The theology returns at this point with a sharper demand. A community can speak of humility and still reserve every important decision to its leaders. It can praise self-emptying while asking the injured to surrender the claim that would cost it money. It can describe unity as sacred while treating departure as betrayal. Within the theological reading proposed here, the credible question concerns what authority relinquishes when the people it serves disagree with it.")
("v1018", "item", "v1019")
("v1017", "value", "v1018")
