("v1053", "scalar", "This is the intuition behind calling trust part of a relational field. It is directed, contextual, and time-dependent. An estimate needs at least an observer, a counterpart, a domain, a component of expectation, and a time. A possible notation is T[i,j,d,k,t]: what i expects of j in domain d, concerning component k, at time t. Reliability in resource administration, willingness to acknowledge error, and competence in adjudication need not move together.")
("v1052", "item", "v1053")
("v1051", "value", "v1052")
