("v1102", "type", "String")
("v1102", "scalar", "Aggregation can destroy these distinctions. A community with high average reported trust may contain a small group whose complaints are consistently blocked. Two networks can have the same average while differing sharply in who holds resources and who can exit. A useful report should retain group-specific conditions and the direction of dependence, rather than treating an average as a complete description.")
("v1101", "item", "v1102")
("v1100", "value", "v1101")
("v1036", "item", "v1095")
