("v1128", "type", "Sequence")
("v1129", "type", "String")
("v1129", "scalar", "The shared-rule scenario instead allows cooperation, delegation, taking, patronage, challenge, and partial repair to interact. A breach can change a resource-reliability estimate. Continued service can change dependence. Dependence can sustain actual compliance even when willing cooperation falls. Taking can finance the resistance to a later challenge. Restitution can reduce a material loss and supply evidence that someone may or may not recognize as repair. The resulting outcome belongs to the interaction of these rules. (")
("v1128", "item", "v1129")
