("v2418", "type", "Entry")
("v2418", "key", "children")
("v2419", "type", "Sequence")
("v2420", "type", "String")
("v2420", "scalar", "There is a further identification problem. A latent expectation can be rescaled so that one curve imitates another. If r is inferred from the behavior it is supposed to explain, apparent support for a cooperation law may be circular. An empirical comparison would need expectations elicited before the decision, dependence measured through actual alternatives and refusal costs, and behavior observed separately. It would also need room for both rules to fail. (")
("v2419", "item", "v2420")
