("v2440", "type", "String")
("v2440", "scalar", "Why does this difference matter to the institutional story? In the modeled resource policy, lower willing cooperation leads to more taking. Some of that taking becomes patronage. More patronage raises the resources required to enforce a challenge. A small difference in a cooperation rule can therefore travel through several relationships and alter whether a formal ruling becomes effective. The extraction policy is as important to examine as the cooperation curve. A different institution might take more from those who cooperate more, or levy a fixed amount independent of cooperation.")
("v2439", "item", "v2440")
("v2438", "value", "v2439")
("v1515", "item", "v2433")
("v2441", "type", "String")
("v2441", "scalar", "\n")
("v1515", "item", "v2441")
("v2442", "type", "Record")
("v2442", "entry", "v2443")
("v2443", "type", "Entry")
("v2443", "key", "tag")
("v2444", "type", "String")
("v2444", "scalar", "p")
("v2443", "value", "v2444")
("v2442", "entry", "v2445")
("v2445", "type", "Entry")
("v2445", "key", "attrs")
("v2446", "type", "Record")
("v2445", "value", "v2446")
("v2442", "entry", "v2447")
("v2447", "type", "Entry")
("v2447", "key", "children")
("v2448", "type", "Sequence")
("v2449", "type", "String")
("v2449", "scalar", "Two selected cases made the sensitivity visible. Case A begins without an outside reserve and allocates a smaller share of taking to patronage. Case B begins with an outside reserve but a larger patronage share. At their nominal settings, the linear rule leaves first-hearing financial margins of +0.019 and +0.002 material tokens respectively. The quadratic rule leaves −0.033 and −0.154. A positive margin permits enforcement within the model; a negative margin blocks it. The cases were selected because the rules reversed the outcome, so they are diagnostic examples rather than an independent confirmation set.")
("v2448", "item", "v2449")
("v2447", "value", "v2448")
("v1515", "item", "v2442")
("v2450", "type", "String")
("v2450", "scalar", "\n")
("v1515", "item", "v2450")
("v2451", "type", "Record")
