("v2454", "type", "Entry")
("v2454", "key", "attrs")
("v2455", "type", "Record")
("v2454", "value", "v2455")
("v2451", "entry", "v2456")
("v2456", "type", "Entry")
("v2456", "key", "children")
("v2457", "type", "Sequence")
("v2458", "type", "String")
("v2458", "scalar", "The +0.002 result is especially instructive. It has the appearance of a definite answer while depending on a very narrow crossing. Lowering the unknown-expectation fallback from 0.50 to 0.49 reverses that nominal linear decision. The fallback is not a measurement of anyone's trust. It is a declared value used when the relevant record remains unknown. A conclusion resting on it should not acquire the authority of a precise empirical estimate.")
("v2457", "item", "v2458")
("v2456", "value", "v2457")
