("v2862", "entry", "v2867")
("v2867", "type", "Entry")
("v2867", "key", "children")
("v2868", "type", "Sequence")
("v2869", "type", "String")
("v2869", "scalar", "This changes the question we can responsibly ask. Instead of asking which rule delivers the preferred verdict at its midpoint, we can ask which interventions retain the desired capacity under both rules and across the admitted uncertainty. That is a more demanding target. It also remains conditional on what the uncertainty set includes. Holding robustly against two candidate mechanisms does not establish robustness against the world. Both mechanisms may be inadequate.")
("v2868", "item", "v2869")
("v2867", "value", "v2868")
