("v3145", "type", "String")
("v3145", "scalar", "Uncertain rates also have to preserve the identity of a trajectory. Suppose one possible path rises from 0 to 10 and another rises from 100 to 110. Both changes are +10. Subtracting the lowest current value from the highest previous value, and vice versa, manufactures an interval from −90 to +110. That interval mixes two different histories. The uncertainty analysis computes changes within each matched path before taking envelopes, preserving the temporal dependence it actually assumes.")
("v3144", "item", "v3145")
("v3143", "value", "v3144")
