("v3154", "scalar", "For a real intervention, delay matters as much as the present rate. If money takes a week to arrive, the relevant question concerns the state in which it can first be used. A simple warning rule projects a falling conservative margin across that lead time. Let L_t be a lower financial assessment based on the declared uncertainty bounds, ℓ the intervention lead time, and ε_m a protective financial floor. Then warn when:")
