("v3407", "type", "Sequence")
("v3408", "type", "String")
("v3408", "scalar", "The first checkpoint creates a revealing difficulty: no earlier observation exists from which to calculate a rate. A policy that requires confirmed erosion cannot act there. Yet the current uncertainty may already include inadequate challenge capacity. Waiting for a derivative can become a refined way to miss an obvious unresolved threshold. Conversely, a falling lower bound should not be treated as proof that actual harm is occurring. The distinction between insufficient assurance and established failure must remain visible.")
("v3407", "item", "v3408")
("v3406", "value", "v3407")
