("v3937", "type", "String")
("v3937", "scalar", "There is a stronger result for the two immediate reserve policies within the unchanged model. An algebraic argument extends preservation over the continuous initial uncertainty box, under both fixed rules. The initial funding requirement remains below the two-token endowment. After the first enforcement and repayment, the royal operating account is emptied. Bounds on post-repair resource expectations and dependence keep the demand for a fresh resource grant below the stipulated issuance threshold. Without new taking or operating funds, royal service cannot restart; dependence cannot increase through that service loop. Patronage remains fixed, while retained review resources and alternative assets do not decline.")
("v3936", "item", "v3937")
("v3935", "value", "v3936")
