("v3945", "type", "Sequence")
("v3946", "type", "String")
("v3946", "scalar", "The conclusion follows from that particular chain of premises. It assumes protected support, immediate delivery, unchanged evidence arithmetic, no new income or shocks, and no depreciation of the alternatives. It also leaves the spare hearing unexercised in the later path. It is not a promise of perpetual solvency under repeated challenges. Making royal service free, lowering the delegation threshold sufficiently, allowing donor withdrawal, or spending the reserve opens the argument again. Some preservation is achieved by interrupting royal service, so any service loss belongs beside the claimed benefit.")
("v3945", "item", "v3946")
