("v4582", "scalar", "Here Succ(B,u) includes every admissible successor information state across the retained mechanisms, parameters, and possible observations. The order of the quantifiers matters. One implementable action must work across the possibilities that remain, rather than a different clairvoyant action being found for each possible world. If action depends on later observations, the observation and update rules must be included. Delays, budgets, authority to act, and the cost of actually exercising another challenge belong in the state or admissible-action set. They cannot be supplied afterward by an optimistic sentence.")
("v4581", "item", "v4582")
("v4580", "value", "v4581")
