("v4600", "type", "String")
("v4600", "scalar", "There is a family resemblance to control-barrier methods, where a controller is constrained to keep a system within a specified set of admissible states. Those methods establish forward invariance under particular dynamics and regularity conditions; they do not decide which social conditions deserve protection. Their useful contribution here is the separation of pursuing an objective from preserving constraints on how that objective may be pursued. Applying their theorems to a social model would require satisfying their premises, rather than borrowing the language of safety as an endorsement. (")
("v4599", "item", "v4600")
