("v4620", "type", "String")
("v4620", "scalar", "That distinction is ethically consequential. Maximizing an aggregate benefit can spend another person's practical capacity to object if that capacity appears only as one weighted term. A constraint-based approach can instead require a specified route of challenge to remain feasible while pursuing other aims. The choice of whose route, which costs, and what floor remains normative and disputable. Mathematics makes that choice inspectable; it cannot make the choice disappear.")
("v4619", "item", "v4620")
("v4618", "value", "v4619")
