("v4678", "scalar", "For an injustice scenario, one might specify unequal access to a review route despite a declared common entitlement. The relevant outcomes could include waiting time, cost, access to evidence, implementation of findings, and the continuing ability to seek another review. No single number needs to announce the justice of the whole institution. The scenario can still reveal that a common procedure systematically becomes unusable for one group.")
("v4677", "item", "v4678")
