("v4724", "scalar", "For a nepotism scenario, family connection might affect appointment, allocation, review membership, or protection from removal. But care for family is not automatically an abuse of delegated office. The key distinctions concern which resources are private, which responsibilities are fiduciary or public, what criteria were promised, and whether related parties can block scrutiny. An administrator's affection is not the same object as the institution's appointment rule.")
("v4723", "item", "v4724")
("v4722", "value", "v4723")
