("v4770", "type", "String")
("v4770", "scalar", "The word coddling is especially easy to misuse. It can refer to avoiding a responsibility someone has freely undertaken and has capacity to perform. It can also be a dismissive name for disability support, legitimate refusal, or ordinary care. A useful scenario would separate capacity, obligation, consent, risk, and who absorbs the cost of nonperformance. The question could then concern whether support expands future options or makes them increasingly dependent on the provider. The model must leave room for continuing support to be appropriate. Independence is not the only valuable human condition.")
("v4769", "item", "v4770")
("v4768", "value", "v4769")
("v4762", "item", "v4763")
("v4761", "value", "v4762")
