("v4783", "type", "String")
("v4783", "scalar", "This last point is fundamental. Dependence is not itself a moral failure, and interdependence is unavoidable. Infants, people who are ill, people with disabilities, and people in ordinary loving relationships may rightly rely on others in enduring ways. A framework that treats every dependence as a defect would merely produce a new ideal person against whom real people could be ranked. The pertinent institutional question is how reliance is governed: whether it can be exploited, whether support survives disagreement, and whether another route exists when the relationship fails.")
("v4782", "item", "v4783")
("v4781", "value", "v4782")
