("v4792", "type", "String")
("v4792", "scalar", "The strongest use of scenarios is therefore comparative and specific. Keep a starting condition visible. Change a mechanism or intervention. Preserve the same uncertainties across the comparison. Examine who bears a cost, which options disappear, and whether a proposed remedy remains available when someone disputes its description. A scenario that flatters every premise of its designer teaches very little about correction.")
("v4791", "item", "v4792")
("v4790", "value", "v4791")
