("v5035", "type", "String")
("v5035", "scalar", "A correction mechanism that accepts these commitments would retain uncomfortable records. It would preserve the complaint as stated, the institution's response, the resources spent, what remained unresolved, and whether implementation occurred. It would record the difference between a person declining to recognize repair and a person obstructing an agreed procedure. It would allow an adverse finding to remain adverse even if the institution later explains what it learned.")
("v5034", "item", "v5035")
("v5033", "value", "v5034")
("v5018", "item", "v5028")
("v5036", "type", "String")
("v5036", "scalar", "\n")
("v5018", "item", "v5036")
("v5037", "type", "Record")
("v5037", "entry", "v5038")
("v5038", "type", "Entry")
("v5038", "key", "tag")
("v5039", "type", "String")
("v5039", "scalar", "p")
("v5038", "value", "v5039")
("v5037", "entry", "v5040")
("v5040", "type", "Entry")
("v5040", "key", "attrs")
("v5041", "type", "Record")
("v5040", "value", "v5041")
("v5037", "entry", "v5042")
("v5042", "type", "Entry")
("v5042", "key", "children")
("v5043", "type", "Sequence")
("v5044", "type", "String")
("v5044", "scalar", "It would also preserve failed predictions. Suppose the model predicts that alternative assets lower dependence, but the assets cannot be used without the original provider. Suppose it predicts cessation after formal revocation, but the office keeps taking. Suppose hearing costs rise during an emergency, peer trust deteriorates under retaliation, or the new funder excludes the people most at risk. Each is a reason to alter the model's account of the mechanism. None should be automatically redescribed as confirmation that the model was wise to mention complexity.")
("v5043", "item", "v5044")
("v5042", "value", "v5043")
("v5018", "item", "v5037")
("v5045", "type", "String")
("v5045", "scalar", "\n")
("v5018", "item", "v5045")
("v5046", "type", "Record")
("v5046", "entry", "v5047")
("v5047", "type", "Entry")
("v5047", "key", "tag")
("v5048", "type", "String")
("v5048", "scalar", "p")
("v5047", "value", "v5048")
("v5046", "entry", "v5049")
("v5049", "type", "Entry")
("v5049", "key", "attrs")
("v5050", "type", "Record")
("v5049", "value", "v5050")
("v5046", "entry", "v5051")
("v5051", "type", "Entry")
("v5051", "key", "children")
("v5052", "type", "Sequence")
("v5053", "type", "String")
("v5053", "scalar", "The evidence required is concrete. Time-stamped accounts can establish when resources became available and when they were spent. Records of actual challenges can distinguish obtaining a finding from securing implementation. Independent descriptions of service alternatives can test whether an asset creates a usable option. Prospective expectation reports can be compared with subsequent events. Former members and people who declined participation may reveal costs that are absent from the accounts of those who stayed. Their silence cannot safely be coded as either satisfaction or dissent.")
("v5052", "item", "v5053")
("v5051", "value", "v5052")
("v5018", "item", "v5046")
("v5054", "type", "String")
("v5054", "scalar", "\n")
("v5018", "item", "v5054")
("v5055", "type", "Record")
("v5055", "entry", "v5056")
("v5056", "type", "Entry")
("v5056", "key", "tag")
("v5057", "type", "String")
("v5057", "scalar", "p")
("v5056", "value", "v5057")
("v5055", "entry", "v5058")
("v5058", "type", "Entry")
("v5058", "key", "attrs")
("v5059", "type", "Record")
("v5058", "value", "v5059")
("v5055", "entry", "v5060")
("v5060", "type", "Entry")
("v5060", "key", "children")
("v5061", "type", "Sequence")
("v5062", "type", "String")
("v5062", "scalar", "Measurement itself has costs. Asking for more evidence can demand time, expose identities, or burden a person who has already absorbed a loss. An institution that insists on perfect identification before accepting any obligation can reproduce the satire with a more conscientious vocabulary. The evidential standard should fit the action and the risk, and uncertainty should remain explicit. A small reversible resource offer and an irreversible exercise of coercion do not require the same warrant.")
("v5061", "item", "v5062")
("v5060", "value", "v5061")
("v5018", "item", "v5055")
("v5063", "type", "String")
("v5063", "scalar", "\n")
("v5018", "item", "v5063")
("v5064", "type", "Record")
("v5064", "entry", "v5065")
("v5065", "type", "Entry")
("v5065", "key", "tag")
