("v5069", "type", "Entry")
("v5069", "key", "children")
("v5070", "type", "Sequence")
("v5071", "type", "String")
("v5071", "scalar", "Neither is precaution automatically benign. Funding one route can confer status on its organizers, steer a dispute into the funder's preferred forum, or use resources needed elsewhere. A protective floor can privilege those who know how to invoke it. A permanent emergency alarm can normalize intervention. These are reasons to retain the cost of the intervention, its limits, and the option to refuse it. The model's proposed object of protection is challenge capacity, including challenge to the intervention itself.")
("v5070", "item", "v5071")
("v5069", "value", "v5070")
("v5018", "item", "v5064")
("v5072", "type", "String")
("v5072", "scalar", "\n")
("v5018", "item", "v5072")
("v5073", "type", "Record")
("v5073", "entry", "v5074")
("v5074", "type", "Entry")
("v5074", "key", "tag")
("v5075", "type", "String")
("v5075", "scalar", "p")
("v5074", "value", "v5075")
("v5073", "entry", "v5076")
("v5076", "type", "Entry")
("v5076", "key", "attrs")
("v5077", "type", "Record")
("v5076", "value", "v5077")
("v5073", "entry", "v5078")
("v5078", "type", "Entry")
("v5078", "key", "children")
("v5079", "type", "Sequence")
("v5080", "type", "String")
("v5080", "scalar", "There are genuine alternatives to the proposal here. A different cooperation mechanism may fit better. Informal mediation may sometimes preserve a relationship better than a funded hearing. Repeated litigation may exhaust people even when money remains. Distributed authority can slow urgent coordination. A useful next comparison would include these alternatives and the harms of intervention, rather than treating the present candidate policies as exhaustive.")
("v5079", "item", "v5080")
("v5078", "value", "v5079")
